        "y0": 0.7689671717171718,
        "x1": 0.882326797385621,
        "y1": 0.855854797979798
      },
      "text": "the above, and since τ2 must ﬁx q1(x), we must have that τ(ζk) = ζl where kp p l = −1. So since τ is a Galois automorphism over K, we must have τ(q1(x)) = q−1(x). This yields that q−1(x) = f(x) −",
      "html": null,
